I tested that idea in a [cut-paper collage study](/design-lab/collage/) using the Mangrove Figma screenshot. One complete view of the work stays visible, with a few cropped fragments around it and a black angular shape behind. The experiment uses the same paper, cobalt and display type as the rest of the site.

This feels promising for selected project covers, an article illustration or an occasional social card. Those are places where a picture can set the pace before the reading begins. Ordinary thumbnails and photographs keep their intact images; navigation and paragraphs keep their clear edges. I have made it an optional figure component for posts, with the main image intact and its caption kept upright. The example below uses a complete library overview with decorative crops from the component-detail screenshot.

